*--- Identify shock time periods using imported Excel data ---

$ontext
 This subsection uses imported data from Excel on start and ending years for the shocks
 to assign shocks to all years within that range. It loops over years and uses two
 two counter parameters to track when the start year is reached (SHKT1) and when the
 final year is reached (SHKTN). Both counters need values of 1 for the shocks to be
 imposed on the model.
 
 Note that shock years can differ across shock areas within the same simulation. For
 example, the years with changes in world export prices (pwe) may differ from the years
 when there is an increase in total factor productivity (alphava).
 
 For shock areas related to closures, it is assumed that all years are active. For example,
 if a particular household is excluded from a savings rates closure adjustment, then it is
 excluded for all simulation years - user cannot change closure rules across years, only
 across simulations.
$offtext

PARAMETER
 SHKT1(SHKAREA,SIMAC,SIM)      counter for identifying starting year for shocks
 SHKTN(SHKAREA,SIMAC,SIM)      counter for identifying final year for shocks
;

PARAMETER SHKCLOS(SHKAREA,SIMAC)    Excel imported data related to closure choices for shock areas /
 com.tax        1
 act.alphaf     1
 act.tax        1
 fac.tax        1
 hhd.save       1
 hhd.tax        1
/;
 

